    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "# ZORR BLATT — UNIFIED ARCHIVE FEED V1\n\nSTATUS = DURABLE FEED / NOT A SECOND SOURCE OF TRUTH\nAUTHORITY = current main + Permanent Archive V1 RAW history\nARCHIVE_WORKFLOW = `.github/workflows/zb-permanent-archive-v1.yml`\nARCHIVE_BRANCH = `zb-archive-v1`\nARCHIVE_ROOT = `hq/archive-v1`\n\n## PURPOSE\nOne durable entry point for evidence produced outside Shared HQ (for example `zorr-blatt-local-executor`, HOME-PC Babylon, HOME-PC ComfyUI), so new LESTER/DUNCAN/JINGO sessions can reconstruct work without chat memory.\n\n## HARD LAW\n`CHAT != ARCHIVE`\n`ACTIONS ARTIFACT != PERMANENT ARCHIVE`\n`EXTERNAL RESULT -> THIS FEED -> PERMANENT ARCHIVE V1 RAW EVENT`\n\nThe issue/comment event itself is automatically preserved byte-for-byte by Permanent Archive V1 and content-addressed by SHA-256. Do not rewrite archived RAW history; corrections append a new superseding comment.\n\n## EVIDENCE ENVELOPE\nEvery external terminal result recorded here should contain only durable coordinates:\n\n- `SOURCE_REPO`\n- `SOURCE_HEAD`\n- `SOURCE_BRANCH`\n- `WORKFLOW_RUN_ID` / `JOB_ID` when applicable\n- `ARTIFACT_ID` / release tag when applicable\n- `FILE_NAME`\n- `SHA256` when physical bytes matter\n- `STATE = PASS | FAIL | BLOCKED | CANDIDATE`\n- `NEXT`\n\nNo prose-only PASS. No chat-only terminal state.\n\n## LARGE BINARY LAW\nDo not grow the Git repository with large binaries. Existing Shared HQ convention remains:\n\n`binary bytes -> GitHub Release asset (immutable/versioned by tag)`\n`metadata -> hq/artifacts/<SHA256>.json`\n\nGitHub Actions artifacts are transport/CI evidence only and may expire; when a binary becomes durable/approved it must be promoted to the permanent binary store and referenced by SHA-256.\n\n## RESTORE ORDER\n1. current `main` Constitution + `AGENTS.md`;\n2. exact task/tracker/PR/workflow evidence;\n3. this feed for external executor coordinates;\n4. original event under `zb-archive-v1/hq/archive-v1` for historical reconstruction/disputes;\n5. binary manifest / release asset when physical bytes are needed.\n\n## BOUNDARY\nThis feed does not replace tracker authority, PR authority, owner gates, QC, or canonical laws. It only guarantees that externally-produced evidence has one recoverable GitHub path into the existing Permanent Archive V1.",
